(* Variant tunnel-none: a further connection joins a tunnel over TLS 1.3 on TCP 443, as the code has it, against an
   attacker that is the network and nothing more (AUD-5, #389; AUD-6, #409). alice has a Tunnel with bob and joins
   connections to it, each in an outer session of its own with the pinned certificate and the binding to its exporter.
   charlie, whose keys the attacker holds, has a Tunnel of his own and may dial bob with any id that he knows, which is
   every id. The server takes the static key of any initiator and compares it with the one of the Tunnel
   (NoiseTunnelJoin). *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | !( TunnelOpen(bob, alice) )
  | !( TunnelOpen(bob, charlie) )
  | !( JoinClient(alice, bob, pin_on, bt_export, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs) )
  | !( JoinServer(bob, bt_export, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs, kc_on) )
  )
